<title>USA: Ameritech, Manpower form strategic alliance.</title>
<headline>Ameritech, Manpower form strategic alliance.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ameritech Corp said Thursday it will form an alliance with Manpower Inc to offer telecommunications staffing services to companies needing temporary help in their call centers.</p>
<p>Ameritech said it will provide call center personnel and performance management during times when companies increase or reduce staff to meet short-term patterns of customer calls. Ameritech said there are 150,000 call centers nationwide.</p>
<p>Ameritech is a local telephone service provider serving customers in five Midwestern states. Manpower provides employment and training to 1.5 million people in 42 countries.</p>
<p>Ameritech stock was up 1/4 Thursday at 55-1/2. Manpower stock was down 3/8 at 31-7/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-877))</p>
